---
interface Props { company: string; mixoRelevance: string; mixvisorRelevance: string; }
const { company, mixoRelevance, mixvisorRelevance } = Astro.props;
const notes = [
  { name:'Product direction', title:'Support changed what we built.', copy:'I’m in support every day, asking customers what works and what doesn’t. Repeated requests for a way to hear from their own visitors led us to build custom forms, so businesses could collect enquiries and feedback through their sites.' },
  { name:'Design engineering', title:'The interface and its state were one job.', copy:'I architected and built Mixo’s Vue 3 application with XState, alongside backend services and shared delivery infrastructure. State modelling helped make complex behaviour explicit as the product expanded from landing pages to multi-page websites.' },
  { name:'Measurement', title:'Use signals to ask better product questions.', copy:'My work includes analytics integrations and monitoring product and website behaviour through PostHog and Cloudflare. I use these signals alongside customer support, rather than treating a chart alone as an explanation of why somebody got stuck.' },
];
---
<div class="application-work">
  <article class="aw-case aw-mixo" aria-labelledby="aw-mixo-title">
    <div class="aw-top"><span>01 / AI PRODUCT</span><span>Co-founder · Product, design &amp; engineering</span></div>
    <div class="aw-grid"><div><span class="aw-brand">mixo<span>.</span></span><h3 id="aw-mixo-title">Making AI<br/>feel simple.</h3><p>I co-founded Mixo to help small businesses get online. My work connects product direction and UX with the frontend, backend, growth and support behind it.</p><div class="aw-tags"><span>Independent ownership</span><span>Vue 3 + XState</span><span>Customer feedback</span></div><p class="aw-hand">from the question to the shipped product.</p></div>
    <figure class="aw-screen"><img src="/work/mixo-prompt.webp" alt="The Mixo product asks a business owner to describe the website they want to create." width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><figcaption>Original product interface from my Mixo case study.</figcaption></figure></div>
    <div class="aw-metrics"><div><strong>500k</strong><span>users within four months of launch</span></div><div><strong>750k+</strong><span>businesses using the platform</span></div><div><strong>3M+</strong><span>websites created</span></div></div>
    <p class="aw-source-note">Reported platform outcomes, not results attributed to one feature or individual.</p>
    <div class="aw-notes">{notes.map(note => <details><summary><small>{note.name}</small><strong>{note.title}</strong><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>{note.copy}</p></details>)}</div>
    <div class="aw-relevance"><small>RELEVANT TO {company.toUpperCase()}</small><p>{mixoRelevance}</p></div>
  </article>
  <p class="aw-bridge">and then there’s the tool I needed in my own studio…</p>
  <article class="aw-case aw-mixvisor" aria-labelledby="aw-mixvisor-title">
    <div class="aw-top"><span>02 / MUSIC SOFTWARE</span><span>Solo design &amp; engineering · Tauri + Vue</span></div>
    <div class="aw-grid"><div><span class="aw-brand">Mixvisor</span><h3 id="aw-mixvisor-title">Built to help me<br/>finish more music.</h3><p>I didn’t need another place to start an idea. I needed a better way to return to the ones I already had. I designed and engineered Mixvisor myself, from that problem in my own studio.</p><div class="aw-tags"><span>Creator workflows</span><span>Desktop application</span><span>Zero to one</span></div><p class="aw-hand">the user and the maker.</p></div>
    <div class="aw-library" data-session-library>
      <div class="aw-library-header"><strong>Session library</strong><span>ILLUSTRATIVE VIEW</span></div>
      <label class="aw-filter">Find an idea<input type="search" placeholder="Search these example sessions" data-session-search /></label>
      <div class="aw-session"><div><b>Night drive</b><small>Ableton Live · Arrangement</small></div><span>126 BPM</span></div>
      <div class="aw-session"><div><b>Side streets</b><small>Logic Pro · Mixing</small></div><span>118 BPM</span></div>
      <div class="aw-session"><div><b>After the rain</b><small>Ableton Live · Idea</small></div><span>122 BPM</span></div>
      <p class="aw-empty" data-session-empty hidden>No matching example sessions.</p>
      <p class="aw-library-note">Example data, not a production screenshot. No access to your files or audio.</p>
      <p class="aw-sr" role="status" data-session-status></p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="aw-notes"><details><summary><small>Product model</small><strong>Sessions, not just files.</strong><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Projects accumulate across folders, drives and DAWs. Mixvisor brings them into one library with workflow status, notes and audio preview, so a producer can recover the context of an unfinished idea.</p></details><details><summary><small>Implementation</small><strong>A desktop product I could carry through myself.</strong><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>I designed the product and its interaction model, then built the Tauri and Vue desktop application. Recognition across major DAWs meant designing around inconsistent source data and existing production habits.</p></details><details><summary><small>Creator understanding</small><strong>A starting point, not a substitute for research.</strong><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>My own workflow gave me a specific problem to start from. I would bring that familiarity to creator research without assuming that every musician works, releases music or measures progress in the same way.</p></details></div>
    <div class="aw-relevance"><small>RELEVANT TO {company.toUpperCase()}</small><p>{mixvisorRelevance}</p></div>
  </article>
  <div class="aw-track-record"><h3>The wider experience.</h3><div><details><summary>Fuzzy Logic Labs <span>2016 to present</span></summary><p>Co-founded the digital agency and startup studio. Work across product direction, design, frontend and backend engineering, growth, support and company operations.</p></details><details><summary>LawPath <span>2016 to 2017</span></summary><p>Product Engineer and Product Manager. Led the company registration product across strategy, design, frontend engineering, third-party APIs and ASIC integration.</p></details><details><summary>CommBank <span>2013</span></summary><p>Led frontend development for the website rebuild, with a 20,000-page migration, frontend architecture, code review and coordination across design and backend teams.</p></details></div></div>
  <details class="aw-sources"><summary>Sources and ownership notes</summary><p>Experience and platform figures are drawn from my published case studies. The creator-analytics study and session-library illustration on this page use fictional data; neither is evidence of a shipped {company} dashboard.</p><a href="https://giles.io/work/mixo/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-astro-prefetch="false">Mixo case study ↗</a><a href="https://mixvisor.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-astro-prefetch="false">Mixvisor product ↗</a><a href="https://giles.io/about/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-astro-prefetch="false">Career history ↗</a></details>
</div>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-session-library]').forEach(root => {
    const search = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-session-search]');
    const rows = [...root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.aw-session')];
    const empty = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-session-empty]');
    const status = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-session-status]');
    search?.addEventListener('input', () => { let count = 0; rows.forEach(row => { row.hidden = !(row.textContent || '').toLowerCase().includes(search.value.trim().toLowerCase()); if (!row.hidden) count++; }); if (empty) empty.hidden = count > 0; if (status) status.textContent = `${count} example sessions found.`; });
  });
</script>
<style>
.application-work{width:100%;max-width:1180px;margin:50px auto 0;font-family:var(--font-body,Arial,sans-serif)}.application-work *{box-sizing:border-box}.application-work [hidden]{display:none!important}.aw-case{border:1px solid #e0e1db;background:#fff;border-radius:24px;padding:clamp(22px,4vw,42px);text-align:left;color:#252823}.aw-top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #e2e3dc;padding-bottom:20px;font:11px var(--font-mono,monospace);color:#636b5c;line-height:1.5}.aw-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.85fr 1.2fr;align-items:center;gap:36px;padding:32px 0}.aw-brand{font-size:32px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.05em}.aw-brand>span{color:#ff2762}.aw-grid h3{font-size:clamp(32px,3.7vw,49px);line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:24px 0 20px;font-weight:800}.aw-grid p,.aw-notes p{font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#586151;margin:0}.aw-tags{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:7px;margin-top:20px}.aw-tags span{font-size:10px;border:1px solid #d3d8cd;border-radius:5px;padding:5px 8px}.aw-grid .aw-hand{font-family:var(--font-hand,cursive);font-size:26px;line-height:1.15;color:#bd2751;margin-top:20px;transform:rotate(-2deg)}.aw-screen{margin:0;background:#f2e7e0;padding:14px;border-radius:16px;border:1px solid #e4d6cc}.aw-screen img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;border-radius:8px}.aw-screen figcaption{font-size:11px;line-height:1.5;margin-top:12px;color:#716459}.aw-metrics{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);border-top:1px solid #e2e3dc;border-bottom:1px solid #e2e3dc;padding:25px 0;gap:18px}.aw-metrics>div{display:grid;gap:8px}.aw-metrics strong{font-size:clamp(29px,5vw,43px);letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:1}.aw-metrics span{font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:#66705e}.aw-source-note{font-size:11px;line-height:1.5;color:#737c6a;margin:10px 0 24px}.aw-notes details{border-top:1px solid #e2e3dc}.aw-notes summary{display:grid;grid-template-columns:136px 1fr 16px;gap:12px;padding:20px 0;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;align-items:center;line-height:1.4}.aw-notes summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.aw-notes summary small{font:10px var(--font-mono,monospace);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em}.aw-notes summary strong{font-size:16px;font-weight:650}.aw-notes details[open] summary>span{transform:rotate(45deg)}.aw-notes p{padding:0 0 24px 148px}.aw-relevance{margin-top:25px;padding:24px;background:#f2f3ed;border-radius:12px}.aw-relevance small{font:10px var(--font-mono,monospace);letter-spacing:.06em}.aw-relevance p{font-size:18px;line-height:1.5;margin:10px 0 0}.aw-bridge{text-align:center;font:clamp(24px,3vw,34px) var(--font-hand,cursive);margin:42px 0;color:#596450;transform:rotate(-2deg)}.aw-mixvisor{background:#23271f;color:#f7f7f1;border-color:#363e2b}.aw-mixvisor :is(.aw-top,.aw-grid p){color:#c8cebf}.aw-mixvisor :is(.aw-top,.aw-notes details){border-color:#4c5742}.aw-mixvisor .aw-notes p{color:#c8cebf}.aw-mixvisor .aw-tags span{border-color:#5b674e}.aw-mixvisor .aw-hand{color:#d2f3aa}.aw-mixvisor .aw-relevance{background:#343c2c}.aw-library{background:#f1f3ed;color:#2d3826;padding:24px;border-radius:16px;min-width:0}.aw-library-header{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px}.aw-library-header>span{font:9px var(--font-mono,monospace)}.aw-filter{display:grid;gap:8px;font-size:12px;margin:22px 0 10px}.aw-filter input{width:100%;min-height:44px;border:1px solid #b6beac;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;background:#fff;font:13px var(--font-body,Arial)}.aw-session{display:flex;gap:12px;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;border-bottom:1px solid #d8dece;padding:18px 0;font-size:14px}.aw-session>div{display:grid;gap:7px}.aw-session small{font-size:11px;color:#627058}.aw-session>span{font:10px var(--font-mono,monospace);white-space:nowrap}.aw-mixvisor .aw-library-note,.aw-mixvisor .aw-empty{font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;color:#59674f;margin:16px 0 0}.aw-track-record{padding:48px 4px 20px;text-align:left}.aw-track-record h3{font-size:28px;letter-spacing:-.03em}.aw-track-record details{border-bottom:1px solid #d4dacb}.aw-track-record summary{font-size:18px;font-weight:600;padding:18px 0;cursor:pointer}.aw-track-record summary span{font-size:12px;font-weight:400;float:right;color:#627058}.aw-track-record p,.aw-sources p{font-size:15px;line-height:1.65;margin:0 0 20px;color:#52604a}.aw-sources{font-size:12px;color:#52604a;padding:24px 0}.aw-sources summary{cursor:pointer;min-height:30px}.aw-sources a{display:inline-block;text-decoration:underline;margin:0 20px 10px 0;text-underline-offset:3px;min-height:24px}.application-work :is(summary,a,input):focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--application-accent,#ff5500);outline-offset:4px}.aw-sr{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip-path:inset(50%)}@media(max-width:760px){.aw-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}.aw-top{flex-direction:column}.aw-notes summary{grid-template-columns:1fr 16px}.aw-notes summary small{grid-column:1/-1}.aw-notes p{padding-left:0}.aw-metrics{gap:12px}.aw-metrics span{font-size:11px}.aw-relevance{padding:18px}.aw-track-record summary span{display:block;float:none;margin-top:5px}.aw-library{padding:18px}}
</style>
